{"name":"Charmed Chalice","hex":"#a1a1a0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"charmed","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Under a magic spell (cast by a charm); bewitched.","Having great good fortune, as though magically wrought."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of charm"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/charmed"},{"term":"chalice","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large drinking cup, often having a stem and base and used especially for formal occasions and religious ceremonies.","A kind of water-cooled pipe for smoking cannabis."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chalice"}],"entries":[{"title":"Charmed","blocks":[{"text":"Charmed is an American fantasy drama television series created by Constance M. Burge and produced by Aaron Spelling and his production company Spelling Television, with Brad Kern serving as showrunner."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/af/Charmedtitlelogo1.jpg/330px-Charmedtitlelogo1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charmed"},{"title":"Chalice","blocks":[{"text":"A chalice is a drinking cup raised on a stem with a foot or base. Although it is a technical archaeological term, in modern parlance the word is now used almost exclusively for the cups used in Christian liturgy as part of a service of the Eucharist, such as a Catholic mass. These are normally made of metal, but neither the shape nor the material is a requirement. Most have no handles, and in recent centuries the cup at the top has usually been a simple flared shape."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/German_-_Chalice_with_Saints_and_Scenes_from_the_Life_of_Christ_-_Walters_44116.jpg/330px-German_-_Chalice_with_Saints_and_Scenes_from_the_Life_of_Christ_-_Walters_44116.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"